# =============================================================
# Line-ending policy — one canonical form, independent of each device's
# core.autocrlf setting.
# =============================================================
# WHY: before 2026-07-27 this repo had no policy at all. Blobs happened to be
# stored LF, but only because this device runs core.autocrlf=true, which
# converts on commit. That is a per-device git *installation* setting, not a
# repo guarantee: a device set to false or input would start committing CRLF
# blobs, and every untouched file would then show as fully rewritten on the
# other machines. A verified renormalize on 2026-07-27 touched 0 existing
# files, confirming this pins the status quo rather than changing it.
#
# NOT the cause of the settings.json conflict-marker corruption -- that was
# .last-cleanup being tracked (see the note in .gitignore). Recorded here so
# the wrong root cause does not get re-derived later.

# Store every text file as LF in the repo AND check it out as LF.
# text=auto lets git detect binary content; eol=lf pins the checkout form.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts: LF is not cosmetic. MSYS2 bash tolerates CRLF, but WSL bash
# and any non-Windows shell fail with "$'\r': command not found".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts are the deliberate exception — cmd.exe needs CRLF.
# None exist today; this rule is here so adding one cannot silently break it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — must never be line-ending normalized or diffed as text.
# The 54 tracked .ttf files are the reason this section is explicit rather
# than relying on text=auto detection alone.
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.eot   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.pyc   binary
